            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of hemosorption and the separate and combined use of obsidan, trental and colpharit on rheological and hemostatic properties of the blood in patients with unstable stenocardia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study of the main hemorheological and hemostatic indices of the blood of 60 patients with unstable angina revealed considerable changes that required correction. The use of hemosorption (HS) produced a positive effect on a clinical course of disease as well as the patients' hemorheological status. However the HS effect maintained for 5 days and the use of drugs was required to prolong a sorption effect. The combined use of propranolol, trental and colpharit made a favorable effect on microcirculation owing to the improvement of rheological, coagulation and fibrinolytic properties of the blood.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
